<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Twelve Days of Christmas (Frederic Austin)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1909</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement that set the standard melody and the current form of the words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Green Chri$tma$ (Stan Freberg)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1958</span><span class="sg-chain-h">snippets of a parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Twelve Gifts of Christmas (Allan Sherman)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Firefly in a Fir Tree (Hilary Knight)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">picture-book version with a mouse as narrator</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Twelve Daze of Christmas (Fay McKay)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1971</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Thirteen Days of Christmas (Jenny Overton)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">children's novel on the origins of the carol</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Pukeko in a Ponga Tree (Kingi Matutaera Ihaka)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1981</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Māori/New Zealand version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Christmas Countdown (Frank Kelly)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">comic retelling of the gifts as received</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Twelve Pains of Christmas (Bob Rivers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1988</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Twelve Days of Christmas, Hawaiian Style (Eaton Bob Magoon Jr., Edward Kenny and Gordon N. Phelps)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">version with new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">On the Twelfth Day... (Wendy Toye)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1955</span><span class="sg-chain-h">comedy short film on the gifts</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">PNC Christmas Price Index</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1984</span><span class="sg-chain-h">yearly index of the cost of the gifts</span></li></ul></section>
